A||||16||ChopTop||Prowler dead||||1||
Z||000000||ChopTop||12-20-2001||01:25 PM||||The Detroit News reported today DCX is ending the Prowler production Febuary 15, 2002.  Approximately 11,000 cars have been sold during the five years of production.  It's built at the Conner Avenue plant in Detroit, Mi.  The last 300 vehicles will be painted a deep candy red.  DCX will replace the Prowler with the Chrysler Crossfire, another automobile that was shown at last years major automotive car shows.  It will be built by Wilhelm Karmann GmbH, no facility or location was mentioned.||||reg||1
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||12-20-2001||01:27 PM||||Got pics of its replacement the Crossfire?  I kinda liked the prowler!  I liked the HOWLER (a aftermarket modded Prowler) better though!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TRiAD||12-20-2001||01:33 PM||||Karmann in in Germany. They built the VW Corrado.<P>The Crossfire prototype was a very interesting vehicle...any idea on engines?<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||12-20-2001||02:02 PM||||They are talking that the Crossfire will share some parts from the Mercedes E-Class sedan and Mercedes transmissions so I'm thinking it will likely use a Mercedes engine.<P>Sad to see the Prowler go, although it was a flagship car for Plymouth to draw in customers they really didn't advertise it well.  I liked the part where the guy that owns 10 of them runs into people all the time that never seen or heard of the car. <P>It was cool tho, and I get a kick out of seeing a few on the road in the summer.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||12-20-2001||02:09 PM||||Check it out here: <A HREF="http://www.car-truck.com/chryed/concept/xfire.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.car-truck.com/chryed/concept/xfire.htm</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.car-truck.com/image/chryed/concept/01/xfire4.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.car-truck.com/image/chryed/concept/01/xfire14.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.car-truck.com/image/chryed/concept/01/xfire34.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.car-truck.com/image/chryed/concept/01/xfire24.jpg"> <P><FONT SIZE="1"><B><BR>Chrysler Crossfire Concept Vehicle Preliminary Specifications <BR>POWERTRAIN <P>Engine: 2.7-liter V-6 supercharged<BR>Estimated Power: 275 bhp. (205 kW) <BR>Estimated Torque: 270 lb.-ft. (366 Nom) <P>Transmission: Five-speed manual transmission <BR>Drive: Rear-wheel drive <P>BODY & SUSPENSION <P>Structure: One-piece carbon fiber body webbed to aluminum frame <P>Suspension <BR>Front: Custom independent short-and-long-arm (SLA) with coil-over-shock setup <BR>Back: Custom independent short-and-long-arm (SLA) with coil-over-shock setup <P>WHEELS & TIRES <P>Wheels <BR>Front: 19" x 8" <BR>Rear: 21" x 11" <P>Tires <BR>Front: P255/40R19 <BR>Rear: P295/35R21 <P>DIMENSIONS & WEIGHT <P>Length: 156.4 in. (3972 mm) <BR>Width: 72.4 in. (1839 mm) <BR>Height: 51.3 in. (1303 mm) <BR>Wheelbase: 102.6 in. (2606 mm) <P>Track <P>Front: 58.3 in. (1481 mm) <BR>Rear: 59.9 in. (1521 mm) <P>Overhang <P>Front: 25.4 in. (645 mm) <BR>Rear: 28.4 in. (721 mm) <P>Weight: 2900 lbs. (1315 kg) <P>ESTIMATED PERFORMANCE <P>0-60 mph. (0-97 kph): 5.8 sec. <BR>Top Speed: 148 mph. (238 kph) <BR>Quarter Mile, Standing Start: 13.9 sec. @ 102 mph. (163 kph) <BR></FONT></B>||||reg||1
