Z||000013||blakeinspace||12-21-2001||02:59 PM||||I hope those employees won't be out of work until the new car starts production... too many layoffs out there as it is.<BR>Dont know how many posters have ever actually driven/ridden a Prowler, but the wife and I did when we were in Vegas at the end of July.  (219.00 a day at Rent-a-vette).  Man that car made a Fiero seem cavernous!  There is a lot less leg room up front (I think they sacrificed leg room for 1 cup holder.... although come to think of it that is exactly 1 more cup holder than our beloved Pontiac has) and that big looking damn rear trunk has NO room.  Example:  we go to the Hoover dam.  We take this tour where you keep the hard hats (mandatory) as souveneers (sp?).  We go back to the Prowler and pop the trunk, and with the top down cant put even 1 hat in the back.  I'm sure we looked real cool in a $40,000 plus ride holding hard hats in our laps (not enough room under your legs either).  In traffic it overheated with the A/C on, and the Intrepid V-6 in there (3.5L if I remember) was way too underpowered for the agressive looks of the car (sound familiar Fiero owners?)  In a hard shift from 1st to 2nd, the back end skipped right, kinda like a FWD torgue steering, only in the back.  We got a LOT of looks and it was fun to pretend to own something you could never afford though.  Maybe next time I will rent their Lambo for a mere $1999.00 a day.  You get a price break if you rent it a week though!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fformula88||12-21-2001||03:33 PM||||Despite its low volume and impracticality, I am still sad to see it go.  It is a very unique car, even for a sports car today.  It got panned recently in Motor Trend for lack of space, etc too, and for someone who might be looking for a sports car to own thats certainly a down side.  At least they were willing to give it a shot!  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||blakeinspace||12-21-2001||04:22 PM||||Formula88... you speak truth.  It is a GOOD thing when manufacturer's offer up something special other than another Camry/Taurus/Galant variant.  I wonder if Prowler ever made Plymouth any money despite its low production numbers?  And even further off the subject.... Playstation's Gran Tourismo has a concept car they call the PT Spyder.  It is a sleek silver mid-engine 2seater that is a lot of fun to play.  Is this just some digital dream or is it legit?  When Plymouth folds would Dodge or Chrylser pick the thing up?  It looks to innovative so therefore it will probably never see the light of production.||||reg||1
Z||000016||kslish||12-21-2001||04:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by blakeinspace:<BR><B>Playstation's Gran Tourismo has a concept car they call the PT Spyder.  It is a sleek silver mid-engine 2seater that is a lot of fun to play.  Is this just some digital dream or is it legit?  When Plymouth folds would Dodge or Chrylser pick the thing up?  It looks to innovative so therefore it will probably never see the light of production.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The PT Spyder was a mid-engined Chrysler concept car a few years back using mostly Neon drivetrain parts and mechanicals to keep the cost down (sound familiar??):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.car-truck.com/image/chryed/detroit/prtspyd2.jpg"> <P>Another interesting thing about the car was that it's plastic body panels weren't painted...the color was molded in.  <P>Read about more about it here: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.car-truck.com/chryed/concept/prspyder.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.car-truck.com/chryed/concept/prspyder.htm</A> <P>Ken S.||||reg||1
